<title>SOUTH AFRICA: KOLOSUS IN TALKS, CAUTIONS SHAREHOLDERS.</title>
<headline>KOLOSUS IN TALKS, CAUTIONS SHAREHOLDERS.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Food producer Kolosus Holdings Ltd said on Thursday U.S. Company Seton had offered its shares in Ladysmith Lindgens Leathers and Lindgens Ladysmith Trimmings to Silveroak Industries Ltd.</p>
<p>The deals would terminate all existing contractual relationships between Silveroak and Seton, the group said.</p>
<p>Kolosus is currently involved in negotiations with Silveroak to acquire 100 percent of the issued shares in the Lindgens companies.</p>
<p>Shareholders were advised to exercise caution in dealing in their shares as the deals could affect the price of Kolosus shares.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
